findings.body:
**Budget-exhausted and cancelled units are labelled `not-started`.**

`accountPlanned` builds every `unstartedUnits` entry with `neverStartedRow` (`src/ops/fix/report.ts:218-241`). That helper always sets `outcome: 'not-started'` on the row and on its failure entry. Only the `reason` text varies between the push sites at Line 888-899, Line 1003-1014 and Line 1175-1179. The outcome is the same in every case.

This produces two wrong labels:
- A unit that returns `budget-exhausted` is persisted as `not-started`, not `exhausted`.
- A unit stopped by the enclosing cancel is persisted as `not-started`, not `cancelled`.

The same label flows into `report.failed` (Line 413-419) and into the PR body's `outstanding` lines (Line 1091-1094). `FixTaskOutcome` already has `'exhausted'` and `'cancelled'` variants, and `plannedTaskRowOf` already maps no-attempt tasks to them. These branchless rows bypass that mapping.

This conflicts with the doctrine. I9 states that "unrun members are marked budget-exhausted, never fabricated as passed or not-applicable."

Fix: store the outcome on each entry and apply it to the row.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
     const unstartedUnits: Array<{
       unit: SweepUnitDispatchInput;
       segments: { kind: string; slug: string; branch: string };
       reason: string;
+      outcome?: FixTaskOutcome;
     }> = [];
@@
         .concat(
-          unstartedUnits.map((entry) =>
-            neverStartedRow(entry.segments, entry.unit.package, entry.reason),
-          ),
+          unstartedUnits.map((entry) => {
+            const row = neverStartedRow(entry.segments, entry.unit.package, entry.reason);
+            const outcome = entry.outcome;
+            if (outcome === undefined) return row;
+            return {
+              ...row,
+              outcome,
+              failures: row.failures.map((failure) => ({ ...failure, outcome })),
+            };
+          }),
         );
```

At the push sites, set `outcome: 'exhausted'` when `status === 'budget-exhausted'`. Set `outcome: 'cancelled'` when `parentSignal?.aborted`, including Line 1175-1179.
</details>

As per coding guidelines: I9 requires that "unrun members are marked budget-exhausted, never fabricated as passed or not-applicable."
